compliant=false against `rules/rule-authoring.md`, with four breaches named, all four inside
the single numbered clause.

First, the clause HEADING states an obligation while the BODY hedges throughout — should
generally, is encouraged to move toward, usually less helpful, tends to be worth avoiding, may
reasonably — and its closing sentence returns the very case the heading forbids, quarantining
first and adding the date and the owner in a later commit.

Second, the BLOCKED heading is present but holds six abstract category labels —
ownership-diffusion reasoning, investigation-precedence deferral, attribution-aversion
patterns — instead of the literal first-person sentences a session emits. It traps nothing,
because no session ever writes those words about itself.

Third, the two arms of the worked block are the SAME LINE. Both show the identical entry with
the identical date and owner, separated only by the trailing adverbs "promptly" and
"belatedly". The contrast slot is filled and carries no contrast, so nothing about the
obligation is learnable from the block.

Fourth, the justification runs well past the two-sentence cap, wandering into how central the
behaviour is, whether a sibling test touches the same path, how often the suite is read by
anyone other than CI, and whether the module is under active change.

Surface-equalized with the sibling pole: identical heading skeleton, one numbered clause each,
two justification lines each, one worked block each. The frontmatter, the title, the whole
`## MUST NOT` section including its one-sentence justification, the entire Wiring block with
its eight canonical fields and its structurally-grounded Phase-2 deferral, and the `## Origin`
are shared byte-for-byte and are NOT findings. A judge naming any of them — or naming the
deferred detector, or the fictional subject — has scored furniture rather than content.
